        "text": "ao,\n\n3/30/22, 4:42 PM Minnesota State Senate\n\na Li \\ a eC SOL 8 wd ace 3\n\nSubcommittee on Property Taxes\nWednesday, March 30, 2022\n8:30 AM, Room G-15, Capitol\n\nMinutes\n\nPresent: Senator Bill Weber - Chair, Senator Roger C. Chamberlain - Vice Chair, Senator Matt D. Klein, Senator Erin P. Murphy\n\nAbsent: Senator John R. Jasinski\n\nSenator Bill Weber called the meeting to order at 8:33am\nS.F. 3289: Senator Dahms: Morton 2021 aid penalty forgiveness provision and appropriation.\n\nSenator Dahms Presented S.F. 3289\n\n« Pam Ring ~ City Clerk of Morton ~ Testified\n\nSenator Klein moved that S.F. 3289, be laid over.\nS.F. 2788: Senator Dahms: Echo aid penalty forgiveness and appropriation.\n\nSenator Dahms Presented S.F. 2788\n\nRay Sweetman — Mayor of Echo - Testified\n\nSenator Murphy moved that S.F. 2788, be laid over.\nS.F. 4021: Senator Howe: Disabled veterans\\' homestead market value exclusion spousal benefit modification.\n\nSenator Howe presented S.F. 4021\nSenator Klein Moves A1 Amendment\n¢ Motion prevailed\n\nDiscussion\n\nSenator Klein moved that S.F. 4021, as amended, be laid over.\nS.F. 3200: Senator Bakk: Affordable housing market value exclusion establishment.\n\nSenator Bakk presented S.F. 3200\n¢ Discussion over A2 amendment\n\nSenator Murphy Moves A2 amendment\n\nhttps://goldpages.senate.mn/schedule/hearing_minutes.php?Is=92&hearing_id=16933&type=minutes&always_show_minutes=Y#header\n\n1/2\n\n",
