        "text": "3/30/22, 4:42 PM Minnesota State Senate\n\n* Motion prevailed\nTestifiers:\n\nKelly Doran ~ Doran Properties Group — Testified\n\nSenator Murphy moved that S.F. 3200, as amended, be laid over.\nS.F. 3882: Senator Weber: Levy limits for certain cities.\n\nSenator Weber presents S.F. 3882\n\n* Cecil Smith — MN Multi Housing Association - Testified\n\n¢ Joe Abraham — Pergola Management - Testified\n\n« Paul Eger - Senior Vice President Governmental Affairs — Testified\n« Dayna Kennedy — Resident - Testified\n\n« Mary Kay Capecchi - St. Paul resident — Testified\n\n* Dan Quillin - Leader of ISAIAH — Testified\n\n« Ginny Deluca — St. Paul resident — Testified\n\nDiscussion\nSenator Klein requested Roll cail to refer S.F. 3882 to Local Government\n\n¢ Senator Weber voted no\n\n¢ Senator Murphy voted yes\n\n* Senator Klein voted yes\n\n* Senator Chamberlain voted no\n\n2-2 Motion did not prevail\n\nDiscussion\n\nSenator Weber moved that S.F. 3882, be laid over.\n\nThe meeting was adjourned at 9:53am\n\na\n\n“wid a Adi apf\n\nSenator Bill Weber, Chair . { Lamont Pyykkonen, jan LAY\n\nhttps://goldpages.senate.mn/schedule/hearing_minutes.php?ls=92&hearing_id=16933&type=minutes&always_show_minutes=Y#header 2/2\n\n",
